<article class="env-proposition" id="EC7B06">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/EC7B06">Proposition <span data-tag="EC7B06">4.4.2.2</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category, and let $p: K \rightarrow \calC $ be a map of simplicial sets. Suppose given a decomposition $K = K' \coprod _{L'} L$, where $L' \rightarrow L$ is a monomorphism of simplicial sets. Suppose further that $p|K'$ has a colimit $X \in \calC $, $p|L'$ has a colimit $Y \in \calC $, and $p|L$ has a colimit $Z \in \calC $. Then one may identify colimits for $p$ with pushouts $X \coprod _{Y} Z$. </p>
</article>